# Channels with only one end, accepted deliberately.
#
# check-wiring.py fails on any channel that is produced but never consumed, or
# consumed but never produced, because that is how the 2026-09-06 outage worked:
# publishes went into a channel with no subscriber and were silently discarded.
#
# An entry here is a claim that a dead end is intentional. If you cannot say why
# in a comment, it is a bug, not an entry.

# Fragments are not ingested in this deployment. The github source produces only
# inbox.pages, inbox.renderers and inbox.rendering-contexts, so nothing ever
# reaches the fragments path: the producer's `fragments` input reads a channel
# with no writer, and the rendering engine's fragment output has no reader.
#
# Vestigial rather than broken — but note these are the SAME shape as the page
# outage. If fragments are ever switched on, wire these two before anything else,
# or fragment ingestion will fail exactly as silently.
relay.fragments
outbox.fragments
